{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2f3d21cb-1782-46e8-b0b8-b96e960a8b40","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_8897768140bd1271","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > specialist_done.partial.json.tmp <<'JSON'\n{\n  \"intent_type\": \"specialist_done\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"confidence\": 0.75,\n    \"domain\": \"enablement_specialist\",\n    \"empty\": false,\n    \"gap_canonical_id\": \"gap.enablement.unknown\",\n    \"new_findings\": [\n      {\"what\": \"The 'unknown' launch failure is NOT a model gap: it is a device-mask contradiction. Magpie builds the server env as os.environ.copy() then overlays benchmark.envs (benchmarker.py:776/800). benchmark.envs pins ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 but never HIP/CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES, so the orchestrator's leaked HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES (multi-id, e.g. '2,3') survives into the vllm child. torch._parse_visible_devices() (torch/cuda/__init__.py:849) hard-raises 'HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES contains more devices than ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES' when len(HIP)>len(ROCR) -> the exception fires during 'import vllm' (vllm/__init__.py:14 -> env_override._patch_inductor_fallback_allow_list -> torch.cuda.is_available()), i.e. before any model code runs. Hence the empty/unknown failure_kind signature.\", \"source\": \"runs/baseline/2fc18296.../server.log + /opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/torch/cuda/__init__.py:833-860 + /opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py:776-960 (reproduced in-session: HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2,3 ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python -c 'import vllm' -> same RuntimeError)\", \"expected_impact\": \"Root cause of 100% of launch failures this session; nothing downstream of 'import vllm' can be reached until reconciled.\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"enablement\",\"rocm\",\"device-visibility\",\"magpie\"]},\n      {\"what\": \"The InferenceX launcher script already implements the correct reconciliation but ONLY fires when HIP is empty: benchmarks/vllm_mi300x.sh:65 'if [ -n \\\"$ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES\\\" ] && [ -z \\\"$HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\\\" ]; then export HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=$(seq -s, 0 n-1)'. An inherited non-empty HIP therefore silently defeats the guard. ROCR re-indexes the visible set to 0..n-1, so the correct HIP value is the LOGICAL range, not the physical ids.\", \"source\": \"/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/.cache/InferenceX@3d55815.../benchmarks/vllm_mi300x.sh:63-68\", \"expected_impact\": \"Tells us the fix is a 1-line-class reconciliation, already sanctioned upstream by the benchmark scripts themselves.\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"magpie\",\"inferencex\",\"rocm\"]},\n      {\"what\": \"Patching the ALLOWED vllm root cannot fix this combo: the serving binary is VLLM_BIN=/usr/local/bin/vllm-wu1w, which imports vllm+torch from /opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages - a tree that is NOT in the allowed source roots. A source patch to /opt/envs/vllm/.../vllm/env_override.py would be inert for the server process (a likely explanation for a prior enablement patch being reverted). The patchable-and-effective surface in the serving path is Magpie itself (/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/Magpie, = manifest.dependencies.magpie.path, which the coordinator imports in-process and which builds the server env).\", \"source\": \"/usr/local/bin/vllm-wu1w (exec /opt/envs/wu1w/bin/python -m vllm.entrypoints.cli.main) + manifest.json dependencies.magpie.path\", \"expected_impact\": \"Redirects the patch from an inert root to the one file that actually composes the crashing env.\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"integration\",\"allowlist\",\"enablement\"]},\n      {\"what\": \"With the device mask reconciled the model itself needs NO enablement code at all: arch resolves natively as Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration, --language-model-only runs it text-only, CompressedTensorsW8A8Int8 selects AiterInt8ScaledMMLinearKernel, GDN runs the Triton/FLA prefill+decode path, and the server reaches /health 200 and emits coherent greedy text ('The capital of France is' -> ' Paris.\\\\nThe capital of Germany is Berlin...'). Verified in-session on port 8911 (boot ~4min incl. compile+graph capture).\", \"source\": \"runs/specialist/b8dc969b.../scratch/run1/server.log + live /v1/completions + /v1/chat/completions responses\", \"expected_impact\": \"Once the env contradiction is gone the combo is fully runnable end-to-end; no HIP/kernel build is needed.\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"vllm\",\"qwen3_5\",\"gdn\",\"w8a8\",\"runnability\"]}\n    ],\n    \"patches_written\": [],\n    \"proposal_set\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"reconcile-device-mask-logical-hip\",\n        \"args_mode\": \"append\",\n        \"atomic\": true,\n        \"extra_envs\": {\"ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES\": \"0\", \"HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\": \"0\", \"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\": \"0\"},\n        \"unset_envs\": [\"HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\", \"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\"],\n        \"kb_evidence\": [], \"pr_evidence\": [], \"source_evidence\": [],\n        \"reason\": \"Removes the leaked multi-id HIP/CUDA mask and re-pins the logical index that ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 already establishes, so torch._parse_visible_devices no longer raises at 'import vllm'. This is byte-for-byte the state the two prior in-session boots reached /health 200 with. atomic=True because the three keys are only self-consistent together (HIP without ROCR would re-target a physical card).\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"residual_questions\": [\"Does orchestration apply variant extra_envs to the BASELINE invocation as well, or only to candidate variants? The sealed baseline cannot produce a non-zero throughput until the device mask is reconciled, so an env-only fix must be applied to both sides to be measurable.\"],\n    \"summary\": \"Diagnosed the 'unknown' gap: it is not a model/code gap but a device-visibility contradiction in the launch env (leaked HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES='2,3' vs yaml ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES='0' -> torch raises inside 'import vllm' before any model code). Reproduced, then booted the real server with the mask reconciled: /health 200 + coherent greedy text, arch Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration + AITER W8A8 INT8 + Triton GDN all native. Now authoring the durable fix in Magpie's env composition (the one allowlisted file on the serving path) plus the env variant.\"\n  }\n}\nJSON\nmv specialist_done.partial.json.tmp specialist_done.partial.json && python3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('specialist_done.partial.json'));print('partial OK')\"\ndate -u","description":"Write checkpoint partial with diagnosis"}}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d04e817-22bd-4007-8bfe-16ebd866a617","uuid":"28e0b4f3-a2ed-4bc0-b301-d3e9929d6592"}
