  filters at the HSA agent layer and re-indexes what survives to ``0..n-1``, so\n    HIP/CUDA must then carry *logical* indices into that reduced set; forwarding\n    the inherited physical ids is wrong twice over. Two distinct launch failures\n    come out of that contradiction, both upstream of any model code:\n\n    * ``len(HIP) > len(ROCR)`` — ``torch._parse_visible_devices()`` raises\n      outright. vLLM calls it during ``import vllm`` (``env_override`` probes\n      ``torch.cuda.is_available()`` at import time), so the server dies before\n      binding a port and the run surfaces only as \"never became healthy\", with\n      nothing model-side to classify.\n    * equal count but out of range (``ROCR=0`` with ``HIP=2``) — does *not*\n      raise; it yields ``torch.cuda.is_available() == False``, so the server\n      fails later and far less legibly on the first device placement.\n\n    A leaked ``CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` alone is enough to reach the first case:\n    vLLM's ``_sync_hip_cuda_env_vars`` copies it onto ``HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` at\n    import, and a HIP/CUDA disagreement is itself a hard ``ValueError`` there.\n\n    The InferenceX launchers already encode the intended rule —\n    ``benchmarks/vllm_mi300x.sh`` derives ``HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0..n-1`` from\n    ``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` — but guard it with ``[ -z \"$HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\" ]``\n    and so cannot fire for a value inherited from the parent environment. This is\n    that same reconciliation, applied at the layer that owns the merge.\n\n    Behaviour is deliberately conservative:\n\n    * acts only on a ROCm host, and only when an effective ROCR mask exists (a\n      config that pins nothing is the launcher's business, not ours);\n    * a mask already valid for the ROCR set is left untouched, so an\n      intentionally multi-card launch stays multi-card;\n    * ROCR is never modified or removed — it is the harness's own pin and is\n      taken as the authority the other masks are reconciled *against*;\n    * on a HIP/CUDA disagreement HIP wins, matching vLLM's own precedence;\n    * any unexpected shape returns ``None`` without touching ``env`` — env\n      hygiene must never itself break a launch.\n\n    Args:\n        env: The child environment about to be handed to the benchmark launcher.\n            Mutated in place when a repair is made.\n\n    Returns:\n        Optional[str]: Description of the repair, or ``None`` when nothing changed.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        if not isinstance(env, dict):\n            return None\n\n        # Match case-insensitively but write through the key that exists, so a\n        # lower-cased entry cannot survive alongside its corrected twin.\n        present: Dict[str, str] = {}\n        for key in env:\n            name = str(key).upper()\n            if name in _ROCM_DEVICE_MASK_VARS:\n                present.setdefault(name, key)\n\n        def _mask(name: str) -> Optional[str]:\n            key = present.get(name)\n            if key is None:\n                return None\n            value = str(env[key] if env[key] is not None else \"\").strip()\n            # Empty string means \"unset\" to both ROCr and vLLM.\n            return value or None\n\n        rocr = _mask(\"ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES\")\n        if rocr is None:\n            return None\n\n        hip = _mask(\"HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\")\n        cuda = _mask(\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\")\n        if hip is None and cuda is None:\n            # Nothing inherited to contradict: the launcher derives HIP itself.\n            return None\n\n        if not _gpu_is_amd():\n            return None\n\n        rocr_ids = [d for d in (p.strip() for p in rocr.split(\",\")) if d]\n        count = len(rocr_ids)\n        if count == 0:\n            return None\n        logical = \",\".join(str(i) for i in range(count))\n\n        def _valid(mask: str) -> bool:\n            \"\"\"True when ``mask`` indexes the re-indexed set without exceeding it.\"\"\"\n            parts = [d for d in (p.strip() for p in mask.split(\",\")) if d]\n            if not parts or len(parts) > count:\n                return False\n            # Non-numeric entries are UUIDs; leave those to the runtime.\n            return all(not d.isdigit() or int(d) < count for d in parts)\n\n        fixed: Dict[str, str] = {}\n        for name, mask in (\n            (\"HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\", hip),\n            (\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\", cuda),\n        ):\n            if mask is not None and not _valid(mask):\n                fixed[name] = logical\n        if (\n            \"HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\" not in fixed\n            and hip is not None\n            and cuda is not None\n            and hip != cuda\n        ):\n            # vLLM raises on the pair disagreeing even when both are in range.\n            fixed[\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\"] = hip\n\n        if not fixed:\n            return None\n\n        changes = []\n        for name, value in fixed.items():\n            key = present.get(name, name)\n            before = env.get(key)\n            env[key] = value\n            changes.append(f\"{name}: {before!r} -> {value!r}\")\n        return (\n            f\"ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES={rocr!r} re-indexes the visible set to \"\n            f\"0..{count - 1}; reconciled \" + \"; \".join(changes)\n        )\n    except Exception:  # pragma: no cover - env hygiene must never break a launch\n        logger.debug(\"device-mask reconciliation skipped\", exc_info=True)\n        return None\n\n\nclass BenchmarkMode:"}}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d04e817-22bd-4007-8bfe-16ebd866a617","uuid":"fe474ec1-552a-416a-bc32-155da6a47d05"}
