moved to the layer that owns the merge - a backport of in-tree sanctioned behaviour, not a new policy.\", \"source\": \"/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/.cache/InferenceX@3d55815.../benchmarks/vllm_mi300x.sh:63-68\", \"expected_impact\": \"Low-risk, precedent-backed shape for the fix.\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"magpie\",\"inferencex\",\"rocm\"]}\n    ],\n    \"patches_written\": [\"patches/001_reconcile_rocm_device_masks.patch\"],\n    \"proposal_set\": [],\n    \"residual_questions\": [],\n    \"summary\": \"Diagnosed the 'unknown' gap as an inherited device-mask contradiction (leaked physical HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES vs the yaml's ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0) that kills the server inside 'import vllm', before any model code - hence no classifiable error. Authored a 158-line insertion into Magpie's _build_local_command that reconciles HIP/CUDA to the logical 0..n-1 set ROCR re-indexes to (a backport of the rule the InferenceX launcher already states but cannot apply to an inherited value). PROVEN END-TO-END: ran the real Magpie serving path under the deliberately-leaked parent env with the patch applied - server reached weight load + 35/35 CUDA-graph capture + /health 200, versus dying at import unpatched. Next (deeper) failure now exposed: the bench CLIENT interpreter /opt/venv/bin/python3 lacks huggingface_hub+transformers (masked until now because every prior attempt died at the server). Patch clears the reported launch gap for baseline AND variants simultaneously, which an env-only proposal cannot do since no baseline number exists yet.\"\n  }\n}\nJSON\npython3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('specialist_done.partial.json.tmp'));print('valid')\" && mv specialist_done.partial.json.tmp specialist_done.partial.json\nprintf '{\"ts\":\"%s\",\"status\":\"running\",\"note\":\"patch PROVEN e2e (server health 200 under leaked env); now clearing deeper blocker: bench-client missing huggingface_hub/transformers\"}\\n' \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" > heartbeat.json; da